#!/usr/bin/env python3
# Stratum — what a PocketMine-MP generation task costs per chunk through PHP,
# split into the C++ the bench already times and everything it leaves out.
# Copyright 2026 the Stratum contributors. SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0
"""M5's generation task, measured through PHP (SPEC §11, "M5's performance bar").

  tools/pmmp-task-cost [--dimensions a,b] [--seeds a,b] [--area cx,cz,r]
      [--scattered on|off] [--warmup n] [--repeat n] [--require-quiet CORES]
      [--quiet-wait S] [--no-counts] [--no-profile] [--count-seeds a,b]
      [--counts-only] [--from OUT] [--stratum-so SO] [--bench BENCH]
      [--out DIR] [--keep-dumps] [--check]

WHAT IT TIMES. The task PocketMine-MP runs to generate a chunk of a Stratum
world, one chunk at a time on one generation thread, through PHP: the
release PHP of tools/pmmp-dev (pmmp/PHP-Binaries php-build-524, PocketMine-MP
5.44.3's own classes from its phar, a server's php.ini: opcache on,
assertions off) with the Release stratum.so (`cmake --preset ext-release`).
ext/pocketmine/task_cost.php is the harness and says in its header exactly
what each segment holds; in short, per chunk:

  (i)   the C++ stratum::pmmp::encodeChunk, as the zend method calls it —
        what stratum_chunk_cost_bench times, here inside PHP;
  (ii)  the zend method's own work round it: marshaling the result into PHP
        arrays (a layer triple per sub-chunk's blocks and biomes, up to 48)
        and putting the fluid updates in the outbox;
  (iii) the plugin's PHP: StratumGenerator::assemble() — palette translation
        to PocketMine-MP state ids, a PalettedBlockArray::fromData per layer,
        the SubChunk and Chunk construction — and the ChunkManager's setChunk;
  (iv)  PocketMine-MP's own task work: the rest of PopulationTask::onRun(),
        chiefly its serialisation of the result (FastChunkSerializer) into
        the task for the main thread; and the worker's cycle collector,
        which AsyncTask::run() calls after every task;

and end to end, the generation thread's whole task, PopulationTask::onRun()
over the plugin's own StratumGenerator plus the collector. The main thread's
side of the hand-back, onCompletion()'s deserialisation, is reported apart:
it is not the generation thread's time. (i) and (ii) are one zend call; the
harness times the call, and a perf profile of that call alone, with call
graphs, gives the share inside stratum::pmmp::encodeChunk and the share
outside it, in instructions and in cycles. LEFT OUT (the harness's header
has the list): AsyncPool's queueing and AsyncTask::run()'s framework (its
SleeperNotifier wake-up), the 3x3 bookkeeping of a population task whose
neighbours are missing, lighting, and the main thread's fluid scheduling.

THE SAME CHUNKS AS THE BENCH, AND ITS OUTPUT AS THE CHECK. Per dimension it
first runs stratum_chunk_cost_bench, built in the same tree with the same
flags as the stratum.so (build/ext-release), over the same seeds and chunks
(the 121 within 5 of chunk (-64, 64) and its 16 scattered ones), with --dump.
That gives the C++-only figure in the same quiet window, and the dump the
harness reads its chunk list from and holds every chunk to: what the zend
method returned, the Chunk PocketMine-MP's task handed back to the main
thread (each block palette the plugin's translation of the C++'s), and the
fluid updates, all identical, for every chunk of both of the harness's
sweeps. A difference fails the run (exit 1). The dumps are vanilla-derived
(SPEC §12): written under OUT/dumps, which ignores itself, and removed at the
end unless --keep-dumps.

THE CLOCKS. Wall and CPU per chunk, each chunk's median over the timed
passes, then median, p10, p90 and mean over chunks, chunks/s as 1000 / mean,
as the bench reports them. Instruction counts (`perf stat -e instructions:u`,
load-independent, valid on a busy box) come from counting runs that switch
perf's events on for one segment alone (`--control`), less the cost of an
empty counting window, measured the same way.

QUIET OR PROVISIONAL, as tools/perf-baseline judges it (its Watch, imported):
other processes' CPU (/proc/stat less this run's process tree) is watched
through every timed half — each bench run and each harness timing run — and
a figure is QUIET only if other processes used at most 0.5 cores on average
and 1.0 over any minute through it; PROVISIONAL otherwise, with the cores
printed. --require-quiet CORES waits before each timed half for the box to
be that quiet, re-checking every 15 s, for at most --quiet-wait seconds
(default 1200) over the whole run; once that is spent, the halves left run
without waiting, each still watched and labelled. A row whose
generation-thread wall time is more than 5% above its CPU time is NOT A
MEASUREMENT (exit 3).

On a busy box, --counts-only measures what load cannot move — the counts,
the profile and the output check — with no timed half, and a later
`--no-counts --no-profile --from OUT` times the halves when the box is
quiet, taking the counts and profile from that OUT (refused unless it
counted the same chunks).

--check is the CTest case (`ctest --preset pmmp-task-cost`; local evidence,
not CI): the overworld and the End at seed 0 over the 9 chunks within 1 of
(-64, 64) and the scattered set, one pass, every check above, every counting
run and the profile if perf is here, and no claim about time.

SKIP (exit 77), naming what is missing: no PocketMine-MP cache
(tools/pmmp-dev), or no fixtures (tools/fetch-vanilla). A missing stratum.so
or bench is a build to run, and an error. OUT defaults to
build/pmmp-task-cost/<UTC time>: timing summaries, logs and perf data only.
"""
import argparse
import csv
import datetime
import importlib.machinery
import importlib.util
import json
import os
import pathlib
import shutil
import subprocess
import sys
import tempfile

REPO = pathlib.Path(__file__).resolve().parent.parent
VERSION = '1.21.11'
DIMENSIONS = ('overworld', 'amplified', 'large_biomes', 'end')
DEFAULT_SEEDS = '0,42,-4172144997902289642'
DEFAULT_AREA = '-64,64,5'
BEST_MS = 35.0
MINIMUM_MS = 100.0
WALL_SLACK = 0.05
# Segments the harness can count, the order they are reported in.
COUNTED = ('window', 'engine', 'plugin', 'pmmp', 'serialize', 'task', 'gc', 'worker', 'completion')
# The profile of the zend call: fixed periods, so samples are in proportion
# to the event (and at most about 45 000 a second between them, under the
# kernel's default cap of 100 000), and a short stack. The marshaling's
# samples are at most three frames from the zend method (measured with 4 KB
# stacks: leaf, addLayer or a zend API function, the method), so 1 KB
# reaches it; a C++ sample too deep to reach encodeChunk is still told
# apart, since it never reaches PHP's own frames either.
PROFILE_EVENTS = ('cpu/instructions,period=1000003/u', 'cpu/cycles,period=200003/u')
PROFILE_STACK = 1024
ENCODE_CHUNK = 'stratum::pmmp::encodeChunk('
ZEND_METHOD = 'zim_Stratum_Dimension_encodeChunk'
# What perf says each time --control switches its events: kept in the log,
# not shown.
PERF_SWITCH = ('Events enabled', 'Events disabled')


def log(message):
    print(f'==> {message}', file=sys.stderr, flush=True)


def die(message, code=1):
    print(f'pmmp-task-cost: {message}', file=sys.stderr)
    sys.exit(code)


def skip(message):
    print(f'SKIP: {message}')
    sys.exit(77)


def perf_baseline():
    """tools/perf-baseline, imported for its Watch: the same reading of what
    other processes ran."""
    path = REPO / 'tools' / 'perf-baseline'
    loader = importlib.machinery.SourceFileLoader('stratum_perf_baseline', str(path))
    spec = importlib.util.spec_from_loader(loader.name, loader)
    module = importlib.util.module_from_spec(spec)
    loader.exec_module(module)
    return module


PB = perf_baseline()


def tee(command, log_path, env=None):
    """Runs @p command, its output kept in @p log_path and shown, but for
    perf's line at each switch of its events."""
    log('$ ' + ' '.join(str(c) for c in command))
    with open(log_path, 'w', encoding='utf-8') as kept:
        process = subprocess.Popen([str(c) for c in command], stdout=subprocess.PIPE,
                                   stderr=subprocess.STDOUT, text=True, cwd=REPO, env=env)
        for line in process.stdout:
            kept.write(line)
            if line.strip() not in PERF_SWITCH:
                sys.stdout.write(line)
                sys.stdout.flush()
        return process.wait()


QUIET_WAITED = [0.0]


def wait_for_quiet(cores, wait_s, what):
    """Watches the machine PB.PROBE_S at a time until other processes use at
    most @p cores, for at most what is left of @p wait_s over the whole run;
    returns the last reading."""
    if cores is None:
        return None
    while True:
        watch = PB.Watch()
        if not watch.available:
            log('cannot read other processes\' CPU here (/proc): not waiting')
            return None
        started = datetime.datetime.now()
        with watch:
            PB.time.sleep(PB.PROBE_S)
        used = watch.summary()['mean_other_cores']
        if used <= cores:
            log(f'before {what}: other processes use {used:.2f} cores (at most {cores})')
            return used
        QUIET_WAITED[0] += (datetime.datetime.now() - started).total_seconds()
        if QUIET_WAITED[0] >= wait_s:
            log(f'before {what}: other processes use {used:.2f} cores, and the run has waited '
                f'{QUIET_WAITED[0]:.0f} s of its --quiet-wait {wait_s:.0f}: measuring anyway, '
                'PROVISIONAL')
            return used
        log(f'before {what}: other processes use {used:.2f} cores, above {cores}; waiting '
            f'({QUIET_WAITED[0]:.0f} of {wait_s:.0f} s)')


def watched(command, log_path, cores, wait_s, what, env=None):
    """Runs @p command under a Watch, after waiting for quiet; returns its exit
    code and the watch's summary."""
    before = wait_for_quiet(cores, wait_s, what)
    watch = PB.Watch()
    with watch:
        rc = tee(command, log_path, env=env)
    summary = watch.summary()
    summary['before'] = before
    return rc, summary


def label(summary):
    if not summary or not summary.get('available'):
        return 'PROVISIONAL (nobody watched)', False
    text = (f'other processes {summary["mean_other_cores"]:.2f} cores mean, '
            f'{summary["peak_other_cores"]:.2f} busiest minute')
    return (('QUIET: ' if summary['quiet'] else 'PROVISIONAL: ') + text), summary['quiet']


# --- perf -------------------------------------------------------------------

def perf_available():
    perf = shutil.which('perf')
    if not perf:
        return None, 'no perf on PATH'
    probe = subprocess.run([perf, 'stat', '-x,', '-e', 'instructions:u', '--', 'true'],
                           capture_output=True, text=True, check=False)
    if probe.returncode != 0 or 'instructions' not in probe.stderr:
        return None, f'perf cannot count instructions:u here: {probe.stderr.strip()[:200]}'
    return perf, None


def fifos(directory):
    control = directory / 'control.fifo'
    ack = directory / 'ack.fifo'
    for fifo in (control, ack):
        if fifo.exists():
            fifo.unlink()
        os.mkfifo(fifo)
    return control, ack


def read_counts(path):
    counts = {}
    with open(path, encoding='utf-8') as handle:
        for row in csv.reader(line for line in handle if line.strip() and not line.startswith('#')):
            if len(row) >= 3 and row[0].strip() not in ('', '<not counted>', '<not supported>'):
                counts[row[2].strip()] = int(float(row[0]))
    return counts


def classify(script_path):
    """Samples of a profile of the zend call by event: under
    stratum::pmmp::encodeChunk (the C++), in the zend method outside it (the
    marshaling), or the counting window's own PHP; and how many C++ samples
    were too deep for their stack to reach the method."""
    tallies = {}
    event = None
    frames = []

    def flush():
        if event is None:
            return
        names = [name for name, _ in frames]
        php = any(dso.endswith('/php') for _, dso in frames)
        if any(name.startswith(ENCODE_CHUNK) for name in names):
            kind = 'cpp'
        elif any(ZEND_METHOD in name for name in names):
            kind = 'marshal'
        elif not php:
            # Truncated: never reached PHP's frames, so not the window's PHP
            # and not the marshaling (whose stacks are shallow): deep C++.
            kind = 'cpp_deep'
        else:
            kind = 'window'
        tally = tallies.setdefault(event, {'cpp': 0, 'cpp_deep': 0, 'marshal': 0, 'window': 0})
        tally[kind] += 1

    with open(script_path, encoding='utf-8', errors='replace') as handle:
        for line in handle:
            line = line.rstrip('\n')
            if not line.strip():
                flush()
                event, frames = None, []
                continue
            if not line[0].isspace():
                flush()
                frames = []
                # "<tid> cpu/instructions,period=N/u:" — which of the two
                fields = line.split()
                name = fields[-1] if fields else '?'
                event = next((e for e in ('instructions', 'cycles') if f'/{e},' in name), name)
                event += ':u'
                continue
            parts = line.strip().split(' ', 1)
            rest = parts[1] if len(parts) > 1 else ''
            cut = rest.rfind(' (')
            frames.append((rest[:cut], rest[cut + 2:-1]) if cut >= 0 else (rest, ''))
    flush()
    return tallies


# --- the run ----------------------------------------------------------------

def parse_args():
    parser = argparse.ArgumentParser(
        description='The PocketMine-MP generation task through PHP, per chunk (see the header).')
    parser.add_argument('--dimensions', default=','.join(DIMENSIONS))
    parser.add_argument('--seeds', default=DEFAULT_SEEDS)
    parser.add_argument('--area', default=DEFAULT_AREA, help='cx,cz,r: the bench\'s spiral')
    parser.add_argument('--scattered', default='on', choices=('on', 'off'))
    parser.add_argument('--warmup', type=int, default=1)
    parser.add_argument('--repeat', type=int, default=3)
    parser.add_argument('--require-quiet', type=float, default=None, metavar='CORES')
    parser.add_argument('--quiet-wait', type=float, default=1200.0, metavar='S')
    parser.add_argument('--no-counts', action='store_true', help='no perf stat counting runs')
    parser.add_argument('--no-profile', action='store_true', help='no perf profile of the zend call')
    parser.add_argument('--counts-only', action='store_true',
                        help='no timed halves: the bench runs once, untimed, for its dumps, and '
                        'only the counting and profiling runs (and their checks) follow — what a '
                        'busy box can still measure')
    parser.add_argument('--from', dest='from_dir', type=pathlib.Path, default=None,
                        help='take the instruction counts and the profile from an earlier run\'s '
                        'OUT where this run makes none (--no-counts, --no-profile)')
    parser.add_argument('--count-seeds', default=None,
                        help='the seeds the counting runs use (default: --seeds)')
    parser.add_argument('--stratum-so', type=pathlib.Path,
                        default=REPO / 'build' / 'ext-release' / 'ext' / 'stratum.so')
    parser.add_argument('--bench', type=pathlib.Path,
                        default=REPO / 'build' / 'ext-release' / 'tools' / 'analysis' /
                        'stratum_chunk_cost_bench')
    parser.add_argument('--out', type=pathlib.Path, default=None)
    parser.add_argument('--keep-dumps', action='store_true')
    parser.add_argument('--check', action='store_true',
                        help='the CTest case: a short run of every check, no claim about time')
    args = parser.parse_args()
    if args.check:
        args.dimensions = 'overworld,end'
        args.seeds = '0'
        args.area = '-64,64,1'
        args.warmup = 0
        args.repeat = 1
        args.require_quiet = None
    try:
        args.seed_list = [int(s) for s in args.seeds.split(',')]
        args.count_seed_list = ([int(s) for s in args.count_seeds.split(',')] if args.count_seeds
                                else args.seed_list)
        cx, cz, radius = (int(v) for v in args.area.split(','))
    except ValueError:
        die('--seeds and --count-seeds are comma-separated integers, --area cx,cz,r')
    args.spiral = (cx, cz, radius)
    args.dimension_list = args.dimensions.split(',')
    for name in args.dimension_list:
        if name not in DIMENSIONS:
            die(f'unknown dimension {name!r} ({", ".join(DIMENSIONS)})')
    if any(s not in args.seed_list for s in args.count_seed_list):
        die('--count-seeds must be among --seeds: the counting runs read the bench\'s dumps')
    if args.warmup < 0 or args.repeat < 1:
        die('--warmup is at least 0 and --repeat at least 1')
    if args.counts_only and (args.no_counts and args.no_profile):
        die('--counts-only with neither counts nor a profile measures nothing')
    return args


def reused_report(args):
    """--from: the earlier run's report, refused unless it measured the same
    chunks: its seeds include the counting seeds, and its square, scattered
    set and dimensions are this run's."""
    if args.from_dir is None:
        return None
    path = args.from_dir / 'report.json'
    if not path.is_file():
        die(f'--from: no report.json in {args.from_dir}')
    report = json.loads(path.read_text(encoding='utf-8'))
    if tuple(report.get('area', ())) != args.spiral or report.get('scattered') != args.scattered:
        die(f'--from: {args.from_dir} measured the square {report.get("area")} with scattered '
            f'{report.get("scattered")}, not {list(args.spiral)} and {args.scattered}')
    for name in args.dimension_list:
        entry = report.get('dimensions', {}).get(name)
        if entry is None:
            die(f'--from: {args.from_dir} has no {name}')
        counted = entry.get('count_seeds') or report.get('seeds')
        if sorted(counted or []) != sorted(args.count_seed_list):
            die(f'--from: {args.from_dir} counted {name} at seeds {counted}, not '
                f'{args.count_seed_list}')
    return report


def preflight(args):
    """SKIP without the PocketMine-MP cache or the fixtures; an error without
    the binaries."""
    pmmp_dev = REPO / 'tools' / 'pmmp-dev'
    probe = subprocess.run([str(pmmp_dev), 'check-cache'], capture_output=True, text=True,
                           check=False)
    if probe.returncode == 77:
        skip(probe.stdout.strip().removeprefix('SKIP: '))
    if probe.returncode != 0:
        die(f'tools/pmmp-dev check-cache: {(probe.stdout + probe.stderr).strip()}')
    fixtures = pathlib.Path(os.environ.get('STRATUM_FIXTURES_DIR') or REPO / '.fixtures')
    root = fixtures / VERSION
    if not (root / 'worldgen' / 'noise_settings').is_dir() or not (root / 'biome_parameters').is_dir():
        skip(f'no vanilla version root at {root}; run tools/fetch-vanilla (or set '
             'STRATUM_FIXTURES_DIR)')
    for path, what in ((args.stratum_so, 'stratum.so'), (args.bench, 'stratum_chunk_cost_bench')):
        if not path.is_file():
            die(f'no {what} at {path}: STRATUM_PHP_CONFIG=$(tools/php-dev --print-config) cmake '
                '--preset ext-release && cmake --build --preset ext-release --target stratum_php '
                'stratum_chunk_cost_bench')
    return root


def harness(args, root, dimension, dumps, spiral_chunks, extra, seeds=None):
    return [str(REPO / 'tools' / 'pmmp-dev'), 'task-cost', '--stratum-so', str(args.stratum_so),
            '--version-root', str(root), '--',
            f'--dimension={dimension}', f'--seeds={",".join(str(s) for s in (seeds or args.seed_list))}',
            f'--dumps={dumps}', f'--spiral-chunks={spiral_chunks}'] + extra


def count_segments(args, root, dimension, dumps, spiral_chunks, out, perf):
    """One perf stat run per segment: instructions and cycles per chunk, less
    the empty window's."""
    work = pathlib.Path(tempfile.mkdtemp(prefix='counts-', dir=out))
    control, ack = fifos(work)
    raw = {}
    for segment in COUNTED:
        stat = out / f'count-{dimension}-{segment}.csv'
        report = out / f'count-{dimension}-{segment}.json'
        command = [perf, 'stat', '-x,', '-e', 'instructions:u,cycles:u', '-D', '-1',
                   '--control', f'fifo:{control},{ack}', '-o', str(stat), '--'] + harness(
            args, root, dimension, dumps, spiral_chunks,
            ['--warmup=1', '--repeat=1', f'--count={segment}', f'--perf-control={control},{ack}',
             f'--json={report}'], seeds=args.count_seed_list)
        rc = tee(command, out / f'count-{dimension}-{segment}.log')
        if rc != 0:
            die(f'the counting run for {dimension} {segment} failed (see '
                f'{out / f"count-{dimension}-{segment}.log"})')
        data = json.loads(report.read_text(encoding='utf-8'))
        raw[segment] = {'counts': read_counts(stat),
                        'windows': sum(r['windows'] for r in data['runs']),
                        'enables': sum(r['enables'] for r in data['runs'])}
    shutil.rmtree(work, ignore_errors=True)
    window = raw['window']
    per_enable = {event: window['counts'].get(event, 0) / max(1, window['enables'])
                  for event in ('instructions:u', 'cycles:u')}
    result = {'per_window_overhead': per_enable, 'segments': {}}
    for segment in COUNTED[1:]:
        entry = raw[segment]
        tasks = max(1, entry['windows'])
        result['segments'][segment] = {
            event: (entry['counts'].get(event, 0) - per_enable[event] * entry['enables']) / tasks
            for event in ('instructions:u', 'cycles:u')}
        result['segments'][segment]['tasks'] = entry['windows']
    return result


def profile_engine(args, root, dimension, dumps, spiral_chunks, out, perf):
    """The zend call alone, profiled with call graphs: the shares inside and
    outside stratum::pmmp::encodeChunk, by instructions and by cycles."""
    work = pathlib.Path(tempfile.mkdtemp(prefix='profile-', dir=out))
    control, ack = fifos(work)
    data = work / 'perf.data'
    seed = args.count_seed_list[0]
    events = [argument for event in PROFILE_EVENTS for argument in ('-e', event)]
    command = [perf, 'record', *events, '--call-graph', f'dwarf,{PROFILE_STACK}',
               '-D', '-1', '--control', f'fifo:{control},{ack}', '-o', str(data), '--'] + harness(
        args, root, dimension, dumps, spiral_chunks,
        ['--warmup=1', '--repeat=1', '--count=engine', f'--perf-control={control},{ack}'],
        seeds=[seed])
    rc = tee(command, out / f'profile-{dimension}.log')
    if rc != 0:
        die(f'the profiling run for {dimension} failed (see {out / f"profile-{dimension}.log"})')
    script = work / 'perf.script'
    with open(script, 'w', encoding='utf-8') as handle:
        rc = subprocess.run([perf, 'script', '-i', str(data), '-F', 'tid,event,ip,sym,dso'],
                            stdout=handle, stderr=subprocess.DEVNULL, check=False).returncode
    if rc != 0:
        die(f'perf script could not read the profile of {dimension}')
    tallies = classify(script)
    shutil.rmtree(work, ignore_errors=True)
    result = {'seed': seed, 'events': {}}
    for event, tally in tallies.items():
        cpp = tally['cpp'] + tally['cpp_deep']
        inside = cpp + tally['marshal']
        result['events'][event] = dict(tally, cpp_share=cpp / inside if inside else None,
                                       marshal_share=tally['marshal'] / inside if inside else None)
    return result


def figure(table, segment, clock='wall'):
    entry = (table or {}).get(segment, {}).get(clock, {})
    return entry if entry.get('available') else None


def fmt(entry, key='mean_ms', digits=3):
    return f'{entry[key]:.{digits}f}' if entry else '-'


def mean_of(table, segment, clock='wall'):
    entry = figure(table, segment, clock)
    return entry['mean_ms'] if entry else None


def millions(value):
    return f'{value / 1e6:.3f}M' if value is not None else '-'


def verdict(mean_ms):
    if mean_ms is None:
        return '-'
    if mean_ms <= BEST_MS:
        return f'meets the best case ({BEST_MS:.0f} ms/chunk)'
    if mean_ms <= MINIMUM_MS:
        return f'between the minimum ({MINIMUM_MS:.0f}) and the best case ({BEST_MS:.0f})'
    return f'BELOW the minimum ({MINIMUM_MS:.0f} ms/chunk)'


def share(profile, event, key):
    entry = (profile or {}).get('events', {}).get(event)
    return entry.get(key) if entry else None


def summarise_dimension(name, bench, php, counts, profile, watches, reused_from=None):
    """The dimension's rows, its problems (a row that is not a measurement),
    and whether both its timed halves were quiet. Without @p php (no timed
    halves) the rows carry instruction counts alone."""
    dimension = bench['dimensions'][name]
    bench_all = dimension['all'] if php is not None else {}
    table = php['all'] if php is not None else {}
    bench_label, bench_quiet = label(watches.get('bench'))
    php_label, php_quiet = label(watches.get('php'))
    chunks = bench['spiral']['chunks'] + bench['scattered_chunks']
    lines = [f'{name} ({dimension["noise_settings"]} / {dimension["biome_source"]}); seeds '
             f'{", ".join(str(s) for s in bench["seeds"])}; {chunks} chunks each']
    if php is None:
        lines.append('  no timed halves (--counts-only): instruction counts and the profile only')
    else:
        lines += [f'  bench half {bench_label}', f'  PHP half   {php_label}']
    if reused_from:
        lines.append(f'  instruction counts and the profile taken from {reused_from}')
    segments = (counts or {}).get('segments', {})

    def instructions(segment):
        return segments.get(segment, {}).get('instructions:u')

    def measured(title, source, segment, instr=None):
        return (title, figure(source, segment), figure(source, segment, 'cpu'), instr)

    def scaled(title, kind):
        """A part of the zend call: its time and its counted instructions,
        each times the profile's share of samples in that event."""
        wall, cpu = mean_of(table, 'engine'), mean_of(table, 'engine', 'cpu')
        cycles = share(profile, 'cycles:u', kind)
        instr = share(profile, 'instructions:u', kind)
        engine_instr = instructions('engine')
        return (title,
                {'mean_ms': wall * cycles} if wall is not None and cycles is not None else None,
                {'mean_ms': cpu * cycles} if cpu is not None and cycles is not None else None,
                engine_instr * instr if engine_instr is not None and instr is not None else None)

    rows = [
        measured('C++ alone: the bench\'s encodeChunk e2e (same build)', bench_all, 'e2e'),
        measured('(i)+(ii) the zend call (encode())', table, 'engine', instructions('engine')),
        scaled('  (i) C++ encodeChunk, from PHP [profile share]', 'cpp_share'),
        scaled('  (ii) zend marshaling + fluid put [profile share]', 'marshal_share'),
        measured('(iii) the plugin\'s PHP (assemble() + setChunk())', table, 'plugin',
                 instructions('plugin')),
        measured('(iv) PocketMine-MP\'s task work (rest of onRun)', table, 'pmmp',
                 instructions('pmmp')),
        measured('  of which serializeTerrain, alone', table, 'serialize', instructions('serialize')),
        measured('(iv) the worker\'s cycle collector', table, 'gc', instructions('gc')),
        measured('PopulationTask::onRun, end to end', table, 'task', instructions('task')),
        measured('= the generation task, end to end', table, 'worker', instructions('worker')),
        measured('main thread: onCompletion (deserialise), apart', table, 'completion',
                 instructions('completion')),
    ]
    lines.append(f'  {"":52} {"wall mean":>10} {"median":>8} {"p10":>8} {"p90":>8} '
                 f'{"CPU mean":>9} {"chunks/s":>10} {"instr/chunk":>12}')
    for title, wall, cpu, instr in rows:
        rate = f'{1000 / wall["mean_ms"]:.1f}' if wall and wall.get('mean_ms') else '-'
        spread = [fmt(wall, key) if wall and key in wall else '' for key in
                  ('median_ms', 'p10_ms', 'p90_ms')]
        lines.append(f'  {title:52} {fmt(wall):>10} {spread[0]:>8} {spread[1]:>8} {spread[2]:>8} '
                     f'{fmt(cpu):>9} {rate:>10} {millions(instr):>12}')

    problems = []
    for what, source, segment in (('the generation thread', table, 'worker'),
                                  ('the bench thread', bench_all, 'e2e')):
        wall, cpu = figure(source, segment), figure(source, segment, 'cpu')
        if wall and cpu and wall['mean_ms'] > (1 + WALL_SLACK) * cpu['mean_ms']:
            problems.append(f'{name}: {what} was descheduled: its wall time is '
                            f'{wall["mean_ms"] / cpu["mean_ms"]:.3f}x its CPU')
    worker = figure(table, 'worker')
    bench_e2e = figure(bench_all, 'e2e')
    engine = figure(table, 'engine')
    if worker and engine:
        added = worker['mean_ms'] - engine['mean_ms']
        lines.append(f'  the generation task less its zend call — the PHP and PocketMine-MP round '
                     f'it: {added:+.3f} ms/chunk ({100 * added / worker["mean_ms"]:.2f}% of the task)')
    if worker and bench_e2e:
        through = worker['mean_ms'] - bench_e2e['mean_ms']
        lines.append(f'  the task through PHP less the C++ alone (separate runs): {through:+.3f} '
                     f'ms/chunk ({100 * through / bench_e2e["mean_ms"]:+.2f}%)')
    if worker:
        lines.append(f'  against the bar: the whole task {verdict(worker["mean_ms"])} — '
                     f'{"QUIET" if bench_quiet and php_quiet else "PROVISIONAL"}')
    if profile:
        engine_wall = mean_of(table, 'engine')
        for event, entry in sorted(profile['events'].items()):
            inside = entry['cpp'] + entry['cpp_deep'] + entry['marshal']
            text = (f'  profile of the zend call, {event}, seed {profile["seed"]}: {inside} samples, '
                    f'{entry["marshal"]} in the zend method outside encodeChunk')
            if inside and event == 'cycles:u' and engine_wall is not None:
                # a Poisson count's rough 95% interval, as time
                low = max(0.0, entry['marshal'] - 2 * entry['marshal'] ** 0.5)
                high = entry['marshal'] + 2 * max(1.0, entry['marshal']) ** 0.5
                text += (f' ((ii) {1000 * engine_wall * low / inside:.1f} to '
                         f'{1000 * engine_wall * high / inside:.1f} us/chunk)')
            text += (f'; {entry["cpp_deep"]} C++ samples too deep for the stack copy to reach '
                     f'encodeChunk, {entry["window"]} in the counting window\'s own PHP, left out')
            lines.append(text)
    if counts:
        overhead = counts['per_window_overhead']
        lines.append(f'  instruction counts: {segments.get("engine", {}).get("tasks", 0)} counted '
                     f'tasks a segment, less an empty counting window\'s '
                     f'{overhead["instructions:u"]:.0f} instructions per switch')
    return lines, problems, php is not None and bench_quiet and php_quiet


def main():
    args = parse_args()
    root = preflight(args)
    perf, why_not = perf_available()
    if perf is None and not (args.no_counts and args.no_profile):
        log(f'no instruction counts or profile: {why_not}')
    stamp = datetime.datetime.now(datetime.timezone.utc).strftime('%Y%m%dT%H%M%SZ')
    out = args.out or (REPO / 'build' / 'pmmp-task-cost' / stamp)
    if args.out is None:
        out = out.resolve()
    if args.check and args.out is None:
        out = REPO / 'build' / 'pmmp-task-cost' / 'check'
        shutil.rmtree(out, ignore_errors=True)
    out.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)
    dumps = out / 'dumps'
    log(f'writing to {out}')

    report = {'tool': 'tools/pmmp-task-cost', 'stamp': stamp, 'machine': PB.machine(),
              'load_average_start': PB.load_average(), 'seeds': args.seed_list,
              'area': list(args.spiral), 'scattered': args.scattered, 'warmup': args.warmup,
              'repeat': args.repeat, 'check': args.check, 'dimensions': {}}
    lines = []
    problems = []
    failures = []
    all_quiet = True
    reused = reused_report(args)
    cx, cz, radius = args.spiral
    for name in args.dimension_list:
        watches = {}
        bench_json = out / f'bench-{name}.json'
        bench_command = [args.bench, root, '--dimensions', name, '--seeds',
                         ','.join(str(s) for s in args.seed_list), '--spiral', f'{cx},{cz},{radius}',
                         '--scattered', args.scattered, '--json', bench_json, '--dump', dumps]
        if args.counts_only:
            # Its dumps alone: one untimed pass.
            rc = tee(bench_command + ['--warmup', '0', '--repeat', '1'], out / f'bench-{name}.log')
        else:
            rc, watches['bench'] = watched(
                bench_command + ['--warmup', str(args.warmup), '--repeat', str(args.repeat)],
                out / f'bench-{name}.log', args.require_quiet, args.quiet_wait, f'the {name} bench')
        if rc != 0:
            die(f'the bench failed for {name} (see {out / f"bench-{name}.log"})')
        bench = json.loads(bench_json.read_text(encoding='utf-8'))
        spiral_chunks = bench['spiral']['chunks']

        php = None
        if not args.counts_only:
            php_json = out / f'php-{name}.json'
            rc, watches['php'] = watched(
                harness(args, root, name, dumps, spiral_chunks,
                        [f'--warmup={args.warmup}', f'--repeat={args.repeat}', f'--json={php_json}']),
                out / f'php-{name}.log', args.require_quiet, args.quiet_wait,
                f'the {name} task through PHP')
            if not php_json.is_file():
                die(f'the harness wrote nothing for {name} (see {out / f"php-{name}.log"})')
            php = json.loads(php_json.read_text(encoding='utf-8'))
            if rc != 0 or php.get('failures'):
                failures.extend(php.get('failures') or [f'{name}: the harness exited {rc}'])

        counts = None
        if perf and not args.no_counts:
            counts = count_segments(args, root, name, dumps, spiral_chunks, out, perf)
        profile = None
        if perf and not args.no_profile:
            profile = profile_engine(args, root, name, dumps, spiral_chunks, out, perf)
        reused_from = None
        if reused is not None:
            entry = reused['dimensions'][name]
            if counts is None and entry.get('counts'):
                counts, reused_from = entry['counts'], str(args.from_dir)
            if profile is None and entry.get('profile'):
                profile, reused_from = entry['profile'], str(args.from_dir)

        dimension_lines, dimension_problems, quiet = summarise_dimension(
            name, bench, php, counts, profile, watches, reused_from)
        lines.extend(dimension_lines + [''])
        problems.extend(dimension_problems)
        all_quiet = all_quiet and quiet
        report['dimensions'][name] = {'bench': bench['dimensions'][name], 'php': php,
                                      'counts': counts, 'profile': profile, 'watches': watches,
                                      'count_seeds': args.count_seed_list,
                                      'counts_from': reused_from}
        if not args.keep_dumps:
            for seed in args.seed_list:
                (dumps / f'{name}_seed{seed}.dump').unlink(missing_ok=True)

    report['load_average_end'] = PB.load_average()
    report['failures'] = failures
    report['not_a_measurement'] = problems
    machine = report['machine']
    header = [
        f'The PocketMine-MP generation task through PHP, {stamp}',
        f'machine: {machine["cpu"]}, {machine["hardware_threads"]} hardware threads, governor '
        f'{machine["governor"]}, boost {machine["boost"]}',
        f'PHP: pmmp/PHP-Binaries php-build-524 (PocketMine-MP 5.44.3), stratum.so {args.stratum_so}; '
        f'one generation thread; {args.warmup} warm-up pass(es), {args.repeat} timed',
        f'load average (the record only): start {report["load_average_start"]}, end '
        f'{report["load_average_end"]}',
        ('no timed halves (--counts-only): instruction counts and profiles only' if args.counts_only
         else 'every half QUIET' if all_quiet
         else 'PROVISIONAL: a half was not quiet (each says which)'),
        'ms/chunk over every chunk of every seed, each chunk its median over the timed passes; '
        'instr/chunk from counting runs',
    ]
    if args.check:
        header.append('--check: a check of the instrument, not a measurement')
    if failures:
        header.append('OUTPUT CHECK FAILED: ' + '; '.join(failures))
    else:
        header.append('output check: every chunk of every sweep identical to the C++\'s (the '
                      'bench\'s dump), through PocketMine-MP\'s task and back')
    if problems:
        header.append('NOT A MEASUREMENT: ' + '; '.join(problems))
    summary = '\n'.join(header + [''] + lines)
    print(summary)
    (out / 'summary.txt').write_text(summary + '\n', encoding='utf-8')
    (out / 'report.json').write_text(json.dumps(report, indent=2, default=str) + '\n',
                                     encoding='utf-8')
    log(f'written: {out / "summary.txt"}, {out / "report.json"}')
    if failures:
        return 1
    if problems and not args.check:
        return 3
    return 0


if __name__ == '__main__':
    sys.exit(main())
